The Problem:
Design an Intelligent LLM Gateway & Router
Design an in-memory LLM Gateway that intercepts incoming user prompts, processes them through optimization layers, and routes them
to the best available LLM provider based on a chosen strategy.

Core Requirements:
Multi-Provider Abstraction: Support multiple upstream AI models (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, or a local Llama model) via a unified interface.
Semantic Caching: Before hitting a costly LLM, check an in-memory semantic cache. If a previous prompt is semantically similar (e.g., proximity score > 90%),
return the cached answer to save time and money.
Token Rate Limiting: Implement a token-bucket rate limiter per API Key based on the estimated token size of the prompt, not just request counts.
Resilience (Circuit Breaker & Fallback): If a provider fails repeatedly or gets rate-limited by the upstream service, trip a circuit breaker and
automatically fall back to an alternative model.
Dynamic Routing Strategies: Support switching between routing strategies: Lowest Cost, Lowest Latency, or Strict Priority (Failover).

